id: pm-rl-e20d
title: "pm-rl: an RL programme as tracked project data"
description: "An RL programme is one of the most context-heavy things an agent can run, and today its context lives in a dashboard, a folder of JSON and shell history: not reviewable, not merge-safe, and not available to the agent deciding what to train next. pm-rl makes the programme itself a tracker. Two pm properties do the real work. Metric logging is append-only and so is pm history, which unions losslessly under concurrent writers on separate branches, so two agents sweeping on two branches never lose rows. And runs form a dependency graph pm already models and queries, so the question that actually costs teams weeks - which results does this reward-spec change invalidate - is a reachability query rather than a feature."
type: Epic
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:28.906Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:43:14.058Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "Every item type registers with typed fields under the host schema; a run's metric series is only ever written to history; two concurrent runs on two branches merge to the union of both series against real git branches; leaderboard and invalidate answer from the dependency graph; 100 percent line, branch, function and docstring coverage"
body: ""
